{"type":"message","id":"010329e7","parentId":"2391c912","timestamp":"2026-03-11T22:02:41.221Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ah, so `sessions.json` is a metadata index file for OpenClaw sessions. It contains information about each active/recent session including:\n- Session ID\n- Model info\n- Token counts\n- Skills snapshot\n- System prompt report\n- Origin/channel info\n- Skill/tool statistics\n- Authentication profiles\n\nIt's essentially a registry/manifest that tracks session state and configuration.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"`sessions.json` is a **session metadata index** for OpenClaw. It tracks:\n\n**Location:**\n- `/home/exouser/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/sessions.json`\n- `/home/exouser/.openclaw/agents/other/sessions/sessions.json`\n\n**What it contains:**\n\n1. **Session info** — Session ID, creation/update timestamps, model used\n2. **Token tracking** — Input, output, total tokens consumed\n3. **Skills snapshot** — All available skills and their configurations\n4. **System prompt report** — Character counts, truncation info, workspace file inventory\n5. **Origin metadata** — Provider, surface (webchat, Discord, etc.), chat type\n6. **Authentication profile** — Which API key config is being used\n7. **Session file reference** — Points to the actual JSONL log file\n\nIt's essentially a **registry** that OpenClaw uses to:\n- Track active sessions\n- Monitor token usage\n- Store configuration state\n- Remember which skills/tools were available\n- Manage session recovery/persistence\n\nThe actual **conversation history** is in the `.jsonl` file (the JSONL I pointed out earlier), while `sessions.json` is the **index/metadata** about that session."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","usage":{"input":12,"output":378,"cacheRead":21487,"cacheWrite":4374,"totalTokens":26251,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0018900000000000002,"cacheRead":0.002