{"type":"message","id":"a9e620b2","parentId":"2dd050b3","timestamp":"2026-03-11T22:50:18.222Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking when sessions.json is used. Let me think about the typical usage patterns in OpenClaw:\n\nBased on what I saw in the sessions.json file, it appears to be:\n1. A metadata index that OpenClaw reads/writes to manage sessions\n2. Contains session state, token counts, configuration\n3. Points to the actual JSONL conversation logs\n\nWhen would it be used:\n- Session startup/recovery - to load session state\n- Token tracking - to keep running totals\n- Session listing - to show available sessions\n- Configuration changes - to update skill/tool info\n- Model/auth switching - to track overrides\n- Cache management - it tracks cache hit/miss metrics\n\nLet me provide a practical explanation of when and how OpenClaw uses this file.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"`sessions.json` is used during these key moments:\n\n## Session Lifecycle\n\n1. **Session startup/recovery**\n   - OpenClaw reads `sessions.json` to find active sessions\n   - Loads the session state (model, auth profile, skills, token counts)\n   - Resumes from the last known state\n\n2. **Session list operations**\n   - When you run `sessions_list` or check active sessions\n   - OpenClaw scans `sessions.json` to show available sessions with metadata\n\n3. **Token accounting**\n   - After each message, OpenClaw updates the `totalTokens`, `inputTokens`, `outputTokens` in `sessions.json`\n   - Used for billing/quota tracking\n   - Visible when you check `/status`\n\n4. **Model/auth switching**\n   - When you override the model or auth profile mid-session\n   - OpenClaw updates `authProfileOverride`, `authProfileOverrideSource` in `sessions.json`\n   - Persists your preferences\n\n5. **Skill/tool discovery**\n   - Stores a snapshot of available skills and tools at session start\n   - Used to avoid re-scanning the filesystem every message\n   - Speeds up tool invocation\n\n6. **System prompt reporting**\n   - Records when the system prompt was generated, which files were injected, truncation warnings\n   - Useful for debugging \"why wasn't X included?\" issues\n\n7. **Cache tracking**\n   - Records `cacheRead`/`cacheWrite` metrics (for prompt caching if enabled)\n   - Shows if Claude's KV cache is being reused efficiently\n\n## When You Don't See It\n\n- During a **single one-shot run** (no persistent session)\n- In temporary sub-agent spawns\n- When operating in isolated mode without session persistence\n\nIt's essentially OpenClaw's **session checkpoint file** — a quick lookup table instead of parsing JSONL logs each time."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","usage":{"input":10,"output":620,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":26145,"totalTokens":26775,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0031000000000000003,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.03268125,"total":0.035791250000000004}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773269410940}}
